  "description": "The **SampleGenerator** is designed to generate sample files based on user input. It accepts the metadata types **typeA** and **typeB**, and depends on two external components, **dep1** and **dep2**. When the generator runs it first asks the user for an **outputPath** (a simple\u2011type question) with the prompt \u201cWhere should the output be generated?\u201d \u2013 the answer is created by the **PathFactory**. The expected response is a string, defaulting to \u201c./output\u201d. Users may choose the predefined option \u201cDefault Path\u201d (response\u202f=\u202fdefault) or \u201cCustom Path\u201d (response\u202f=\u202fcustom). This question is only presented when **dep1** is available, the simple condition **simpleCondition** holds, and the environment is **dev**. The generator will then iterate over **itemList**, retrieving each element by its **id**, with the accompanying text \u201cIterate over items\u201d; this iteration has no additional conditions.  \n\nGenerated files are placed in the **src** and **test** directories. The template variable **author** is set to \u201cJohn\u00a0Doe\u201d. One file is created from the template **templates/main.tpl**, destined for **src/main.js**, and described as the \u201cMain application file\u201d. This file is included only when **dep1** is present, the simple condition **includeMain** is satisfied, and the environment is **prod**."
